  <h1>Getting Started</h1>
  <p>In the first 20 minutes: create the folder structure, fill <code>SECURITY.md</code>, populate the core files in order, and run your first session in the right mode sequence.</p>

  <h2>Step 1 — Copy the starter kit</h2>
  <p>ADDF provides a standard folder structure that makes the operating model visible.</p>
  <img src="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/images/11_Starter kit structure.png" alt="Starter Kit Structure" />
  <ul>
    <li>The core project brain files at the root</li>
    <li>A <code>docs/</code> folder for architecture documentation</li>
    <li>A <code>research/</code> folder for Research Mode output</li>
    <li>A <code>planning/</code> folder containing backlog and sprint subfolders</li>
    <li>A <code>src/</code> folder where Develop Mode writes code</li>
  </ul>
  <blockquote><strong>Rule:</strong> The folder structure should make the operating model visible.</blockquote>

  <h2>Step 2 — Fill SECURITY.md first</h2>
  <p><code>SECURITY.md</code> defines what is and is not safe to load into an AI session. Fill the "never load" list for your project before populating any other file (e.g. <code>.env</code>, credentials).</p>
  <blockquote><strong>Rule:</strong> Fill SECURITY.md before loading files into an AI session.</blockquote>

  <h2>Step 3 — Populate the core files in order</h2>
  <p>The core files form a dependency chain. Fill them in this sequence:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><code>SECURITY.md</code></li>
    <li><code>AGENTS.md</code></li>
    <li><code>DOMAIN.md</code></li>
    <li><code>STATE.md</code></li>
    <li><code>COMMANDS.md</code></li>
    <li><code>DECISIONS.md</code></li>
    <li><code>QUESTIONS.md</code></li>
    <li><code>RISKS.md</code></li>
  </ol>
  <blockquote><strong>Rule:</strong> If a model needs to know it later, write it to the project brain.</blockquote>

  <h2>Step 4 — Your first session</h2>
  <p>A new project starts with this mode sequence: Research Mode → Design Mode (project memory) → Design Mode (sprint pack) → Develop Mode (dry run) → Develop Mode (implementation) → Design Mode (review & state).</p>
  <img src="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/images/10_First-session onboarding flow.png" alt="First Session Onboarding Flow" />
  <blockquote><strong>Rule:</strong> Declare the mode before the model acts.</blockquote>
</DocsLayout>
